usage: pool_progress.py [-h] {init,plan,apply,migrate-preview} ...

Company-pool loop progress reducer and recovery CLI (W05-AUDIT-LOOP). A small,
pure state machine for the pool-loop campaign described in references/company-
pool-loop.md. The reducer folds one observation at a time into an ``audit-
pool-progress/1`` state and proposes the next action for a native harness to
dispatch. It never starts agents or providers, never schedules work, never
keeps a parallel cost ledger, and never evaluates research quality: structural
records_complete stays distinct from four independent review conclusions.
Read-only reuse of P7 primitives: audit_run validation helpers and its
Redactor for every persisted artifact. Duplicate call costs are already
deduplicated by document_status_join.py; this tool only stores call ids and
refs, with unknown cost/usage kept null. State files are written through a
staged-file atomic replace guarded by a short-held OS-level lock; a crash
leaves either the old or the new complete JSON and a locatable ``.pool-
progress-`` orphan, never a torn file.

positional arguments:
  {init,plan,apply,migrate-preview}
    init                create a new pool-loop state
    plan                dry-run one observation
    apply               fold one observation atomically
    migrate-preview     preview an old campaign

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
